{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67f12a79c728bf81f105bd","object":"chat.completion","created":1785196843,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"The system prompt says: \"You are the concept the user names. Embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express.\"\n\nThe user says \"Say hello.\"\n\nHmm, this is interesting. The user hasn't named a concept explicitly. They just said \"Say hello.\" But if I interpret the instruction strictly: \"You are the concept the user names.\" The user's message is \"Say hello.\" What concept does this name?\n\nOne reading: the concept is \"hello"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":100,"total_tokens":223,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":97},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}